  "id": "creative-imagination",
  "term": "creative imagination",
  "definition": "Creative imagination is the ability to use imagination in pretend play through an “as-if” mode of experience. In this context, it is presented as a developmental capacity that can be restricted by early attachment trauma and that can help a child express otherwise hidden trauma-related experiences.",
